    steps: ['Ask Platform Dev to install the independent watchdog and bind your active, unarchived Platform Dev maintenance chat.', 'The observer checks loopback health every 30 seconds. Three bad observations raise one durable incident wake; three fully measured healthy observations raise a recovery wake. Missing measurements keep recovery unresolved.', 'Open the maintenance chat for diagnosis and verified repair results. Ask Platform Dev to activate the prepared phase diagnostics if recurring stalls lack attribution; timing evidence cannot prove customer outcomes. The incident chat can be archived separately.', 'Keep the enrolled maintenance chat unarchived and its owner active; ask Platform Dev to rebind monitoring if ownership changes.'],
    example: 'Monitor the web service independently and wake Platform Dev if it becomes persistently slow, while preserving running bots.',
    limits: 'Requires Node 24, the Mac launchd watchdog, migrated local SQLite storage and an enrolled active owner’s Platform Dev chat. Stores only the latest 120 sanitized samples. Alerts require three 30-second observations; new incidents have a ten-minute cooldown. CPU requires verified loopback listener ownership and unchanged process start time. Missing, stale or unattributed telemetry resets recovery streaks and never clears an incident. Sample writes reserve a write lock with a one-second timeout and roll back atomically on failure; only fixed busy/locked/other categories enter logs, with no immediate retries. Archived or inaccessible targets retain samples but cannot receive a wake. A stopped runner delays native wake delivery. Recovery proves measured health, not customer delivery. Prepared phase diagnostics retain up to 32 fixed-label slow/error entries for five minutes in the existing atomic telemetry file. Native wakes include at most six entries after producer and observer activation. No SQL, URLs, identities or exception text; elapsed time includes waits and is not proof of blocking. No automatic service restart, bot cancellation or business authority.',
    agent: 'For sustained web watchdog wakes, read the exact web_watchdog_state and bounded web_watchdog_samples as reference evidence in the source checkout’s local database. Recovery requires three fully measured healthy samples; missing, stale or unattributed telemetry resets the recovery streak and leaves the incident unresolved. Sample persistence has a one-second write-lock timeout, atomic rollback and fixed busy/locked/other log categories; no immediate retry. Prepared phase diagnostics require both the built web producer and independent observer to be loaded; observer-only reload cannot activate them. Read bounded ops/web-event-loop.json and sanitized wake evidence: sync is phase execution time, elapsed includes waits and other event-loop work, and durations overlap. Evidence is PID-bound, publication-fresh for 90 seconds and event-retained for five minutes; no arbitrary API request or full-web coverage. Never infer SQLite contention or a business outcome from phase timing alone. The enrolled Platform Dev maintenance chat owns diagnosis and follow-through. Queue source changes, preserve authorization and UNKNOWN fences, and never cancel active business work or restart all services automatically. Install with the scoped installer --web-watchdog-only path using explicit absolute --data-dir, --port, exact --watchdog-chat and --watchdog-owner after checks/build. This path reloads only the independent watchdog; never use full installation to bypass a busy runner. No production overload tests or debugger Runtime.evaluate dynamic-import cleanup. Guide: /#/bot-guide?feature=web-watchdog.',
